; GLQuakeTexModeNull -- GLQuake's texture filter (Video Options > Texture
; filter, 2026-11-22) on the null card: config.cfg keeps it as the command
; "gl_texturemode <mode>", and the next start sets it again.
; Start 1 sets Sharp (GL_NEAREST_MIPMAP_LINEAR) on the command line and
; ends after a timedemo (which writes config.cfg); its config.cfg must hold
; "gl_texturemode GL_NEAREST_MIPMAP_LINEAR". Start 2 only asks: it must
; print GL_NEAREST_MIPMAP_LINEAR (from config.cfg), then "bad filter name"
; for a wrong one. The staged config.cfg goes back as it was (the A4000D
; runners send it: a left-over Sharp would change their timings).
; The menu row itself needs eyes on the card (the null card draws nothing).
; Needs: gmake glquake glquake-data rgl-lib.
; LIMIT 900
FailAt 1000
Wait 12
Stack 1000000
Echo "=== machine ===" >DEV:Test/auto.log
CPU >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Copy DEV:Quake/id1/config.cfg DEV:Test/config.cfg-keep QUIET
Delete >NIL: DEV:Test/texmode#?
CD DEV:Quake
Assign LIBS: DEV:Libs/RadeonGL ADD
Echo "=== start 1: Sharp, then a timedemo ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
GLQuake -anycpu -stdout -nosound -nocdaudio -noudp -nolan -timedemoquit +gl_texturemode GL_NEAREST_MIPMAP_LINEAR +gl_texturemode +timedemo demo1 >DEV:Test/texmode1.log
Echo "start 1 rc=$RC" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Search DEV:Test/texmode1.log "MIPMAP" NONUM >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Search DEV:Test/texmode1.log "frames" NONUM >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Echo "=== its config.cfg ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Search DEV:Quake/id1/config.cfg "texturemode" NONUM >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Echo "=== start 2: the mode it starts with, a wrong name ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
GLQuake -anycpu -stdout -nosound -nocdaudio -noudp -nolan -timedemoquit +gl_texturemode +gl_texturemode GL_BOGUS +timedemo demo1 >DEV:Test/texmode2.log
Echo "start 2 rc=$RC" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Search DEV:Test/texmode2.log "MIPMAP" NONUM >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Search DEV:Test/texmode2.log "bad filter" NONUM >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Assign LIBS: DEV:Libs/RadeonGL REMOVE
Copy DEV:Test/config.cfg-keep DEV:Quake/id1/config.cfg QUIET
Echo "=== config.cfg back ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Search DEV:Quake/id1/config.cfg "texturemode" NONUM >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Echo "=== done ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Echo >DEV:Test/AutoDone done
